7} :question/id #uuid "51473619-1294-5307-bfc0-3377a609fc5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-54215" :question/problem "![](images/63/63102dc32e44d75681b95ca5570c737224d7fd887d7c86d2b5c7a1e41a26c9f3.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(4,-4)$ and the point $X(-4,2)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{{(4-(-4))}^{2}+{(-4-2)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-4)^{2}+(y-(-4))^{2} & =(10)^{2} \\\\ (x-4)^{2}+(y+4)^{2} & =100\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088292 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9c351e4-8bd6-5e57-9b6f-32dc18b88bd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x + 1)^{2} + (y + 2)^{2} = 10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086407} {:answer/id #uuid "ceb055af-6e86-5af2-9d4e-27f5372d988c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x + 1)^{2} + (y - 2)^{2} = 10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086408} {:answer/id #uuid "0e091c04-e028-5876-b964-f681d5d46426" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x + 1)^{2} + (y - 2)^{2} = \\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086409} {:answer/id #uuid "5b7da5f6-d41c-5640-809e-40b797691500" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x - 1)^{2} + (y + 2)^{2} = 10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086410} {:answer/id #uuid "5cfb2715-4047-59fb-923f-fb6f02e15f87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x - 1)^{2} + (y + 2)^{2} = \\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086411}] :answer-field/id #uuid "737a60c6-d0a0-5ba1-836e-5c4dc48c0d4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086406}] :question/id #uuid "b799a937-531d-51f5-bb46-daea903429ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-72616" :question/problem "![](images/9e/9e905d98eafd51cd455811dc9b84fbca74f45dedb7fd7363e9dd97c953b3170a.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(-1, 2)$ and the point $X(2, 3)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088311 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0576cbfe-64f6-5bc3-a016-f311431b8cc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(2,3)$ and radius is $6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342291} {:answer/id #uuid "2d02910a-922e-5c4c-b5fc-7dd9508107d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-2,-3)$ and radius is $6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342614} {:answer/id #uuid "30c13b16-79f8-5389-b2ee-a0eb671325c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(0,0)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{6}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342645} {:answer/id #uuid "bc241e1f-2741-5d91-8f59-ef85f94eac0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-2,-3)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{6}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343891} {:answer/id #uuid "c972847a-26b8-5b15-aa4d-ff0fb36da0a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(2,3)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{6}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c972847a-26b8-5b15-aa4d-ff0fb36da0a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(2,3)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{6}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344005} :answer-field/id #uuid "89edcb63-a33b-5de5-ba63-aeca3edd3169" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344735}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c280c3e5-8a01-5bfb-b585-89deed38b8eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-7521" :question/problem "What is the center and radius of the circle with equation $(x-2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=6?$" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's compare the general equation to our equation side-by-side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & =6 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & =(\\sqrt{6})^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $a=2,$ $b=3,$ and $r=\\sqrt{6}.$ \n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(2,3)$ and its radius is $\\sqrt{6}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088312 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83750412-13d3-53b5-b710-5024a1954edd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-5,-1)$ and radius is $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086527} {:answer/id #uuid "933eca4a-b650-5a3a-883c-f905c2389a8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-5,-1)$ and radius is $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086528} {:answer/id #uuid "95761f1a-a3e0-5727-9225-0803ad54c6b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(5, 1)$ and radius is $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086529} {:answer/id #uuid "05806bc8-cd02-5c0b-bf54-4f7466a6c0f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(5, 1)$ and radius is $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086530} {:answer/id #uuid "12c0ca05-f49d-5fa0-b7df-8a6667d46198" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-5,-1)$ and radius is $4^{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086531}] :answer-field/id #uuid "7264ccff-1242-5bcf-aa59-50d9a42715cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086526}] :question/id #uuid "0b82b51c-240a-56bc-959f-8619bdcbeea5" :question/math-academy-id "q-7527" :question/problem "What is the center and radius of the circle with equation $(x + 5)^{2} + (y + 1)^{2} = 4$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235496 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ea6a32f-49ef-57a9-b429-d346d779f130" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+{y}^{2}=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234691}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ea6a32f-49ef-57a9-b429-d346d779f130" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+{y}^{2}=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234691} :answer-field/id #uuid "455de079-3c57-5a2c-b063-2ae6c0d12dd7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235041}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "70fc8621-7b34-535c-a0b8-10d27db72e32" :question/math-academy-id "q-167932" :question/problem "Write the equation of this circle in the form $(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a circle with radius $r$  centered at the point $(a,b)$ in rectangular coordinates in standard form is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the circle is centered at $(3,0)$ and the radius of the circle is $r=3$, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-3)^{2}+(y-0)^{2} & ={3}^{2} \\\\ (x-3)^{2}+{y}^{2} & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the circle in rectangular coordinates is \n\n$$\n(x-3)^{2}+{y}^{2}=9.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253292 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f753d8c-60a5-57f8-bdf7-1dfca23922c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250687} {:answer/id #uuid "194d005a-074c-5528-8e5a-5c077edd8e76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250774} {:answer/id #uuid "315ac89d-372a-5365-ae8a-8dbdf9c4b3ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250971} {:answer/id #uuid "85cecc42-57d3-50a8-a690-6891b14e42dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251673} {:answer/id #uuid "b9e225b3-c9f2-51bf-8ede-3befd132f224" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252187}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "315ac89d-372a-5365-ae8a-8dbdf9c4b3ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250971} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf481095-8ecd-5669-92d1-9a4c71b18f2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253136}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1378faa1-06f3-5893-a7e8-8251ca750847" :question/math-academy-id "q-116929" :question/problem "![](images/b6/b69a99c42bcdbd7e6ae3434862019b792da6bea498fd92a36595722d4fb66995.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the circle given above?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFrom the picture, we see that our circle is centered at $C(-4,-3)$ and the radius of the circle is $r=6.$ Therefore, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-4))^{2}+(y-(-3))^{2} & ={6}^{2} \\\\ (x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253301 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cf2e972-6b80-5e52-afb7-0e4c5944055c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250935} {:answer/id #uuid "c20eabe8-bd89-54f4-9981-d68d1fd1e853" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252265} {:answer/id #uuid "cfda17b2-0685-57a1-b791-0077608dabf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252387} {:answer/id #uuid "f12ce672-6885-5af0-9cbb-b55844cce857" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252659} {:answer/id #uuid "f96fbc78-0903-5d5b-8866-617fa9e2ed76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252737}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cfda17b2-0685-57a1-b791-0077608dabf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252387} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc3c07d4-04ac-5acc-abd3-b0629a17016d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253249}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1568b6f8-f70c-51a1-ba2c-b92acb3124ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-117077" :question/problem "![](images/5e/5e138922d95cbcf6cc6ceba4d7695b110f5414e08f2a5e9e2ae2d71bff70ab5d.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the circle given above?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFrom the picture, we see that our circle is centered at $C(2,-3)$ and the radius of the circle is $r=4.$ Therefore, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y-(-3))^{2} & ={4}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253302 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b15e7a5-78ca-5688-a932-a2ff47f3474b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-5)^{2}+{y}^{2}=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250921} {:answer/id #uuid "303b72ca-c041-5f4d-ba88-cfc9252584e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}=49" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250963} {:answer/id #uuid "58063976-49ff-516f-bbee-085c50f0cd83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=49" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251273} {:answer/id #uuid "730971b8-62e4-54a4-a7ef-c3267c982997" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251502} {:answer/id #uuid "cc0cfc11-8f30-57fc-b4eb-7dbd668540da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-5)^{2}+{y}^{2}=49" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "303b72ca-c041-5f4d-ba88-cfc9252584e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}=49" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250963} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8df55f5-2f9b-5f02-9b2c-4736a5b8b86a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253211}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5dd64115-dbeb-5cf8-8fc0-3bacf50a0c2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-117081" :question/problem "![](images/98/9839540667b095cec69ce6ea429aa99b129e90fee26c4adf1f25ffa6019d5067.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the circle given above?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFrom the picture, we see that our circle is centered at $C(-5,0)$ and the radius of the circle is $r=7.$ Therefore, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ {(x-(-5))}^{2}+(y-0)^{2} & ={7}^{2} \\\\ (x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2} & =49.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253303 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2155b67f-cc1d-5498-baae-1a55b610aaeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-5,0)$ and the radius is $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250836} {:answer/id #uuid "26bae4f0-a2ab-5dfc-8621-7bd36660b0cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(0,0)$ and the radius is $\\sqrt{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250884} {:answer/id #uuid "6fffde91-36c3-505d-ad07-5119e9819c6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-5,0)$ and the radius is $\\sqrt{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251467} {:answer/id #uuid "7b723c2e-efc3-562f-8e5d-152539fbaef3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(5,0)$ and the radius is $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251580} {:answer/id #uuid "efc9f639-d769-54cb-a7a3-c5c5c8e2dbce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(5,0)$ and the radius is $\\sqrt{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "efc9f639-d769-54cb-a7a3-c5c5c8e2dbce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(5,0)$ and the radius is $\\sqrt{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252651} :answer-field/id #uuid "895097b3-e59b-5153-97c3-96479b69b34d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253040}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e4a072a8-8d88-5c4f-855b-cd6b51714292" :question/math-academy-id "q-117087" :question/problem "What is the center and the radius of the circle with equation $(x-5)^{2}+{y}^{2}=3?$" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's compare the general equation to our equation side-by-side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-5)^{2}+{y}^{2} & =3 \\\\ (x-5)^{2}+(y-0)^{2} & ={(\\sqrt{3})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $a=5,$ $b=0,$ and $r=\\sqrt{3}.$ \n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(5,0)$ and its radius is $\\sqrt{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253304 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b0c7c14-a555-5e01-8838-765e944ceedf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250784} {:answer/id #uuid "78dc7686-f3de-5b7d-8046-a89585820e9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251556} {:answer/id #uuid "994030d6-5bdf-505c-ac30-a525c985caa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251870} {:answer/id #uuid "a7739a17-e686-57c5-ba6c-a87d9d4e8077" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251995} {:answer/id #uuid "d0408c11-e9e7-55cb-940f-15a1df96ac67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252393}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "994030d6-5bdf-505c-ac30-a525c985caa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251870} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0900e01-a03b-5ddb-af66-ba4873931f4b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253187}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4be1d8bd-eb38-5bfc-b4eb-dd764bc3beed" :question/math-academy-id "q-117096" :question/problem "![](images/16/16d6786a4b1934ed234d4bf0896187aa6e93ec70cf045ddf4b743b1f51eaac2f.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(-4,-3)$ and the point $X(-1,0)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{(-1-(-4))^{2}+(0-(-3))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-4))^{2}+(y-(-3))^{2} & ={(3\\sqrt{2})}^{2} \\\\ (x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =18\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253305 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cb0ea5e-ad3e-596c-a47f-1b2f569400c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250794} {:answer/id #uuid "1dd34dda-6f93-5397-a33e-2a03884b982c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250807} {:answer/id #uuid "b690d28c-7840-5bec-9fea-01836e32189d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252161} {:answer/id #uuid "bff71f03-a6dd-5c42-a982-4c93c6ea8bd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252249} {:answer/id #uuid "dfbf80d1-3ee1-578b-9627-526049a9423e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252527}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b690d28c-7840-5bec-9fea-01836e32189d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252161} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d7781ff-a993-5178-9bac-63ccd91c2ea5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252969}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "014cf060-ee36-5cab-a46b-0c5421540a60" :question/math-academy-id "q-117099" :question/problem "![](images/2b/2bd7e3cb9594623c6f5dc3fad35c33c71df0efe9e80b2053dde33f4ef9080bda.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(-4,-3)$ and the point $X(0,-1)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{(0-(-4))^{2}+(-1-(-3))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-4))^{2}+(y-(-3))^{2} & ={(2\\sqrt{5})}^{2} \\\\ (x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253306 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d30c4f2-1c9b-56aa-b62b-7e9a63a5c394" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250936} {:answer/id #uuid "51ebda4a-c6ab-56ec-a85d-515c28547d71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251224} {:answer/id #uuid "9cde4a0d-d36b-53dd-9c07-256ac68ea24e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251906} {:answer/id #uuid "c3b65520-eb87-5289-bc62-41aa3b67fb30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252285} {:answer/id #uuid "df53c346-071e-5d55-b02f-a149afdcd833" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252522}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df53c346-071e-5d55-b02f-a149afdcd833" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252522} :answer-field/id #uuid "311dd4be-59af-5907-99cb-162e30c5bc61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252890}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "93ab0f69-1e36-5855-80b5-7cee6cddd602" :question/math-academy-id "q-117102" :question/problem "![](images/af/afd2f435a60fbb5a0f0f83c5f8965a74ca107d1ed4b14d03401f7966a323d2f1.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{―}{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(2,4)$ and $(2,0)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(2,4)$ and $Y(2,0),$ we find that the length of the diameter is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{(2-2)^{2}+(4-0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{XY}{2}=\\frac{4}{2}=2.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, we can find the center using the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2})=(\\frac{2+2}{2},\\frac{4+0}{2})=(2,2)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=2$ and center $(a,b)=(2,2),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y-2)^{2} & ={2}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y-2)^{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253307 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23dbf520-5c3b-5b0b-ba2f-9f13812d437b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250862} {:answer/id #uuid "bd2c3273-1427-5200-b8fa-ae62dd0254b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252224} {:answer/id #uuid "f3d74c25-4afb-5a05-86ec-741a51b80fe5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252690} {:answer/id #uuid "f4f229e0-e36c-5d89-bfa3-eb4e80db5b78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252700} {:answer/id #uuid "fb945b04-2597-5034-872d-2f63ecdf08d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252759}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23dbf520-5c3b-5b0b-ba2f-9f13812d437b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250862} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ee3ff0f-0ad3-57b0-80be-ce3303f10b7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253051}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e7556293-0fd9-5aac-b946-74962289d2c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-117103" :question/problem "![](images/08/08653e0cdc9bb404bd7ef193dfc9f1b5c0884002e83dd72cbcbda5779a2363a1.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{―}{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(2,-1)$ and $(2,1)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(2,-1)$ and $Y(2,1),$ we find that the length of the diameter is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{(2-2)^{2}+(-1-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{XY}{2}=\\frac{2}{2}=1.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, we can find the center using the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2})=(\\frac{2+2}{2},\\frac{-1+1}{2})=(2,0)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=1$ and center $(a,b)=(2,0),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y-0)^{2} & ={1}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253308 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1449a778-d0cd-54af-b254-ed3e6cf1e350" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250729} {:answer/id #uuid "210a0d60-0ad2-5c82-bbdf-57fa4f773dd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250833} {:answer/id #uuid "3fbdbf00-5f32-5f31-b62b-8082aac14eb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251080} {:answer/id #uuid "9aa1cebc-2118-57ee-afa4-b243d9a8d486" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251881} {:answer/id #uuid "c79d3915-b972-5b9e-9dbd-ac4105903344" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252320}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c79d3915-b972-5b9e-9dbd-ac4105903344" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252320} :answer-field/id #uuid "8058d059-e858-5260-9048-73a64f45f512" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253024}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "7713e957-0cbe-5d3f-93d1-81e2b678b8a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-117105" :question/problem "![](images/05/0598fca48db1dbfb0cacadcf2ffb5cd987fc4e922fe85585849763fedac1f28e.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{―}{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(-3,0)$ and $(1,-2)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(-3,0)$ and $Y(1,-2),$ we find that the length of the diameter is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{(-3-1)^{2}+(0-(-2))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4\\cdot 4+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4\\cdot 5} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{2}=\\sqrt{5}.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, to find the center we use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2})=(\\frac{-3+1}{2},\\frac{0-2}{2})=(-1,-1)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=\\sqrt{5}$ and center $(a,b)=(-1,-1),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-1))^{2}+(y-(-1))^{2} & ={(\\sqrt{5})}^{2} \\\\ (x+1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2} & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253309 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27146995-40b8-5fb9-a436-de880c16f96b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250890} {:answer/id #uuid "3d3b83a1-785f-569a-9e04-1f4d911a200b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251061} {:answer/id #uuid "6e015f74-e5e1-5e7d-8695-c6dc5c93e9ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251454} {:answer/id #uuid "8e8ee6e0-b5ff-59bc-82f8-2de8c7c6342b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251762} {:answer/id #uuid "b43bb4a8-cb77-5ae2-870d-f55b9e5f7c59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252136}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b43bb4a8-cb77-5ae2-870d-f55b9e5f7c59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252136} :answer-field/id #uuid "94017d7f-a209-5ab8-99c1-91d78574ffbd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253064}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "6610e1ab-73a7-5f4a-8c57-8d6e77beff9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-117106" :question/problem "![](images/0a/0a0820b21672bbf16d2fdb35d708aefc4129fdc81c7594b55af3bd2ef5b8fc0f.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{―}{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(-2,0)$ and $(0,2)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(-2,0)$ and $Y(0,2),$ we find that the length of the diameter is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{(-2-0)^{2}+(0-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{2}=\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, to find the center we use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2})=(\\frac{-2+0}{2},\\frac{0+2}{2})=(-1,1)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=\\sqrt{2}$ and center $(a,b)=(-1,1),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-1))^{2}+(y-1)^{2} & ={(\\sqrt{2})}^{2} \\\\ (x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253310 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34b1554c-96e1-5f34-bd7d-39439e7d2d90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250994} {:answer/id #uuid "3e0c96c8-b6f3-508c-bbce-383fbffc5d73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251069} {:answer/id #uuid "71463607-983f-5491-bdcc-71080d1290aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251480} {:answer/id #uuid "78ba35b2-ca4d-559a-9e58-c33761c27a13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251553} {:answer/id #uuid "dbfbf876-ab7e-5bb9-b30b-9654f0019146" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252487}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34b1554c-96e1-5f34-bd7d-39439e7d2d90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250994} :answer-field/id #uuid "233384c8-214c-54f0-a58a-ee2651d7fa9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252869}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "b6f2966b-20a6-5c34-af5a-1e6c31f128aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-117107" :question/problem "![](images/7f/7f1573d17cb9a603727b644da6598355875b0be4b8c43a382e562155cb7a095c.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{―}{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(-1,-3)$ and $(3,1)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(-1,-3)$ and $Y(3,1),$ we find that the length of the diameter is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{(-1-3)^{2}+(-3-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{4\\sqrt{2}}{2}=2\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, to find the center we use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2})=(\\frac{-1+3}{2},\\frac{-3+1}{2})=(1,-1)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=2\\sqrt{2}$ and center $(a,b)=(1,-1),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+(y-(-1))^{2} & ={(2\\sqrt{2})}^{2} \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2} & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338844 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5fbf4e0c-e58b-5108-bbb0-4fd59e0d8f51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336899} {:answer/id #uuid "716b6ec9-6172-5328-9d80-1420c737a11d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337047} {:answer/id #uuid "a2353a98-7f3f-5dcb-8a84-2f6b9edb5c4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337504} {:answer/id #uuid "cd350b86-92f1-5b47-8195-38e00e0239ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337831} {:answer/id #uuid "feac2e41-7550-5e75-ab07-0ad3fc367bb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338266}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2353a98-7f3f-5dcb-8a84-2f6b9edb5c4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337504} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8cce04b-83c9-5250-85c8-d53e40d3c24a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338613}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4b58a709-693d-534f-9bbe-586e11704f18" :question/math-academy-id "q-70896" :question/problem "![](images/ba/baa279bad56527ad959b2923f25df848396ffc7060c612469d637d4e614117b5.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the circle given above?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFrom the picture, we see that our circle is centered at $C(1,2)$ and the radius of the circle is $r=5.$ Therefore, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2} & ={5}^{2} \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2} & =25.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338845 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a00270e-5e9a-5b54-924d-4ef9bdceca94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337432} {:answer/id #uuid "a825607b-2d15-5682-8738-35632d6078be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337552} {:answer/id #uuid "dac05b17-668c-59f0-a102-93f1f5f12437" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337937} {:answer/id #uuid "ee7cb397-1c3d-5437-80bc-0d25f5c93337" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+3)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338118} {:answer/id #uuid "f4c47c68-de5c-5236-b155-78a447eb8332" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4c47c68-de5c-5236-b155-78a447eb8332" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338171} :answer-field/id #uuid "7718debd-009e-52ad-b486-a85853f1ee0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338482}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "81c6457c-f4fd-58e1-87c0-0244bbebd614" :question/math-academy-id "q-70898" :question/problem "![](images/88/887895a47cf6ce3a6f109f754ef0c46eecaa6d68763baf3a696008e014d231af.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the circle given above?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFrom the picture, we see that our circle is centered at $C(-2,-3)$ and the radius of the circle is $r=8.$ Therefore, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-2))^{2}+(y-(-3))^{2} & ={8}^{2} \\\\ (x+2)^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =64.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338846 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0de6ec9c-a18f-5c39-bba0-7cd4d2c4cbec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(2,2)$ and radius is $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336163} {:answer/id #uuid "261c78a4-aa16-55ca-ba41-03405b8a6a5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-2,-2)$ and radius is $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336391} {:answer/id #uuid "4a82f12d-a5fd-5222-85b3-fbb8dc687319" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-2,2)$ and radius is $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336718} {:answer/id #uuid "b11e1bf4-cbaa-5da1-9b69-039cece23840" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(2,-2)$ and radius is $9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337618} {:answer/id #uuid "bde20a03-ced7-5f44-8882-cfde31bf1343" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(2,-2)$ and radius is $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337719}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bde20a03-ced7-5f44-8882-cfde31bf1343" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(2,-2)$ and radius is $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337719} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e02e2ba-e4d8-5493-866f-036379c2d1ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338385}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ae69cd1b-0a71-523f-826f-ffa9cc343ca4" :question/math-academy-id "q-70900" :question/problem "What is the center and radius of the circle with equation $(x-2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=9?$" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's compare the general equation to our equation side-by-side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2} & =9 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y-(-2))^{2} & ={3}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $a=2,$ $b=-2,$ and $r=3.$ \n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(2,-2)$ and its radius is $3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338851 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07ca118a-c6bd-5450-9425-9c36f7d885b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-3,-3)$ and radius is $5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336095} {:answer/id #uuid "7e77ce24-9b12-5518-b880-fef2d2b5aee7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(3,3)$ and radius is $5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337175} {:answer/id #uuid "c86388d9-fab6-5c9d-8548-47665f65daef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(3,3)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337805} {:answer/id #uuid "daa728ef-76a5-5bdc-bdc9-e5c2963954c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-3,-3)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337935} {:answer/id #uuid "e127089c-cdb2-55d2-9194-95a3353e427e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-3,3)$ and radius is $5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337996}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "daa728ef-76a5-5bdc-bdc9-e5c2963954c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-3,-3)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337935} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e76b9a2-98b8-50ac-be7b-e3fc9f5dc1c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338441}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "82bdb90e-db88-5742-a337-6ee1c028122e" :question/math-academy-id "q-70935" :question/problem "What is the center and radius of the circle with equation $(x+3)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=5?$" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's compare the general equation to our equation side-by-side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x+3)^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =5 \\\\ (x-(-3))^{2}+(y-(-3))^{2} & =(\\sqrt{5})^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $a=-3,$ $b=-3,$ and $r=\\sqrt{5}.$ \n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(-3,-3)$ and its radius is $\\sqrt{5}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338867 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "301aa6a7-5ee2-5a20-9033-4674a143461b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+3)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336492} {:answer/id #uuid "64b4c7ae-6592-5435-9dcf-3efafb11647a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336934} {:answer/id #uuid "7faacc68-2956-5fc6-9e73-4fc524688331" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+3)^{2}-(y+3)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337190} {:answer/id #uuid "8864933a-7a46-5b44-8a98-d9f22b098b5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337262} {:answer/id #uuid "ed738468-0ab1-5dc7-96f4-55c16f6a1c9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+3)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338104}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64b4c7ae-6592-5435-9dcf-3efafb11647a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336934} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6d043a5-1717-5a07-aecc-41e08ef6bda7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338587}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0ffdebd9-641e-5fc7-a83b-a3474a188cc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-70987" :question/problem "![](images/b6/b6a4e9a8f4a1c6dcaaad453b843896f3fc56ae22a37d481dcb4cfe54cc53361d.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{―}{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(7,3)$ and $(-1,3)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is  \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(7,3)$ and $Y(-1,3),$ we find that the length of the diameter is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{{(7-(-1))}^{2}+{(3-3)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64} \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{8}{2}=4.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, to find the center we use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2})=(\\frac{7+(-1)}{2},\\frac{3+3}{2})=(3,3)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=4$ and center $(a,b)=(3,3),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-3)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & ={4}^{2} \\\\ (x-3)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338868 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00e4a49e-453f-5b68-98b1-7a31adb93775" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}-{y}^{2}=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336038} {:answer/id #uuid "450d803a-0dda-576f-ae85-76770d27f4a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+{y}^{2}=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336677} {:answer/id #uuid "7ee14867-8540-55f0-b7a0-7100bebee222" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337181} {:answer/id #uuid "87685e0e-a82f-5609-beee-7cd2ee774d09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+3)^{2}+{y}^{2}=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337255} {:answer/id #uuid "adc4df30-8770-5d9e-9c11-b2f992c2a043" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337592}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ee14867-8540-55f0-b7a0-7100bebee222" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337181} :answer-field/id #uuid "0625c9ee-953d-5a19-becb-0ce059539921" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338285}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "4b08908d-2189-5c82-98e7-76da156bba41" :question/math-academy-id "q-70990" :question/problem "![](images/a6/a6a21dbf4785a270a0ae03066df1f92df73974532f9a75aa8e470cef42ea5e14.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{―}{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(-3,2)$ and $(3,4)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is  \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(-3,2)$ and $Y(3,4),$ we find that the length of the diameter is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{{(-3-3)}^{2}+{(2-4)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-6)^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{40} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4\\cdot 10} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{2\\sqrt{10}}{2}=\\sqrt{10}.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, to find the center we use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2})=(\\frac{-3+3}{2},\\frac{2+4}{2})=(0,3)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=\\sqrt{10}$ and center $(a,b)=(0,3),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-0)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & ={(\\sqrt{10})}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341841 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27f70d2a-fc69-5d4c-8d76-eb29f542cee8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339477} {:answer/id #uuid "6d8195c7-e766-5e8a-9057-7cf807388cde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340095} {:answer/id #uuid "8aa99c96-03d0-5732-b316-93ca22442393" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340366} {:answer/id #uuid "c9082b17-653a-55a6-b4da-3fcc60887456" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340909} {:answer/id #uuid "e3377fdf-0433-59b7-872c-aa80d378fdc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341140}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27f70d2a-fc69-5d4c-8d76-eb29f542cee8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339477} :answer-field/id #uuid "30d50e00-9328-53c1-9634-e13ef473cc3c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341463}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "54aa38dd-d17e-53f7-9a6f-f5bb4a2cb026" :question/math-academy-id "q-72617" :question/problem "![](images/d4/d45a9c753270dfd9186bc16736d1815a11997c88d2f35a0c40f487e6acef66c6.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(-2,3)$ and the point $X(1,-1)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{{(1-(-2))}^{2}+{(-1-3)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-2))^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & ={5}^{2} \\\\ (x+2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341842 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "024d17a6-71d7-5b07-a9f7-4e90925b4266" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339148} {:answer/id #uuid "39733cc5-69a1-5e1d-bebb-7bb234749a05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339644} {:answer/id #uuid "cdc3778a-58ce-553d-acdf-2eca8ef39844" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340954} {:answer/id #uuid "d77e9864-505e-5fbd-9ca7-87866b380248" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341040} {:answer/id #uuid "e5fd184d-c4e9-5208-a605-04a08c3cfd8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341162}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5fd184d-c4e9-5208-a605-04a08c3cfd8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341162} :answer-field/id #uuid "8dcfaa52-1bc6-5a58-9c52-332c3dac793a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341630}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e9071118-1df3-5b01-93dc-2b5f04fcff39" :question/math-academy-id "q-72619" :question/problem "![](images/2f/2ff035f38f5892f61d1eb037c7e39c59c8ec5104babac45224c4902152a0cfaa.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(-1,-3)$ and the point $X(1,1)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{{(1-(-1))}^{2}+{(1-(-3))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-1))^{2}+(y-(-3))^{2} & =(\\sqrt{20})^{2} \\\\ (x+1)^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341843 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44ceba2e-461c-5d6f-94d0-fffabcaa7f4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=\\sqrt{41}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339737} {:answer/id #uuid "67364410-21ff-5ab6-b499-984469e0f0b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340042} {:answer/id #uuid "7e6b7a0c-3051-526a-9636-efd77cb0b591" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+3)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340268} {:answer/id #uuid "c00a31e7-30ad-5958-a723-a2568cb7ceb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=\\sqrt{41}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340844} {:answer/id #uuid "ccdecbe3-6add-5929-86dd-7b81307f2bae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+3)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=\\sqrt{41}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340941}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67364410-21ff-5ab6-b499-984469e0f0b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340042} :answer-field/id #uuid "59370454-96d7-5c69-8869-e408beefd110" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341537}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b538b794-53e2-55d6-941e-f772138f1dd6" :question/math-academy-id "q-72621" :question/problem "![](images/6e/6e68ede9db2528ea607fc6fd63f0ec4ca1c1378982239913ef49153e1cf5b609.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(3,-3)$ and the point $X(-1,2)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{{(-1-3)}^{2}+{(2-(-3))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{41}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-3)^{2}+(y-(-3))^{2} & =(\\sqrt{41})^{2} \\\\ (x-3)^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =41\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393050 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "414d2687-cf0f-5475-b4de-9ae0e2a91b57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-1,-6)$ and radius is $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393052} {:answer/id #uuid "b904b162-87b0-576b-9c8a-3c647aa88565" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-1,-6)$ and radius is $16$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393053} {:answer/id #uuid "e0376e6b-94e1-5393-8f70-58f85be3025d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(1,6)$ and radius is $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393054} {:answer/id #uuid "a1fe974f-7739-5447-8c15-65e11281c360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(1,-6)$ and radius is $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393055} {:answer/id #uuid "1a4bb814-df36-50ef-990c-594eb222e321" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(1,6)$ and radius is $16$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393056}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "414d2687-cf0f-5475-b4de-9ae0e2a91b57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-1,-6)$ and radius is $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393052} :answer-field/id #uuid "85727bd6-7f77-5807-aa8a-f0686b43c486" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393051}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fed78696-d1d3-57b4-8aa2-ab1ef29e5f93" :question/math-academy-id "q-70933" :question/problem "What is the center and radius of the circle with equation $(x+1)^{2}+(y+6)^{2}=16?$" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's compare the general equation to our equation side-by-side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x+1)^{2}+(y+6)^{2} & =16 \\\\ (x-(-1))^{2}+(y-(-6))^{2} & ={4}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $a=-1,$ $b=-6,$ and $r=4.$ \n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(-1,-6)$ and its radius is $4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399933 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6440d02-db02-5883-9248-472636d87c8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(5,-3)$ and the radius is $81$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399935} {:answer/id #uuid "94926a7f-9ef5-5bea-98f4-3362f05a53c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-5,3)$ and the radius is $9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399936} {:answer/id #uuid "fa5c4042-f4c5-57b6-807b-9dcbfece1050" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(5,-3)$ and the radius is $9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399937} {:answer/id #uuid "cc99ae56-0324-5987-9998-2298bc7a275a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-5,3)$ and the radius is $81$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399938} {:answer/id #uuid "2b544bb0-1ba1-5798-982f-f6455ce5b545" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-5,-3)$ and the radius is $9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399939}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94926a7f-9ef5-5bea-98f4-3362f05a53c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-5,3)$ and the radius is $9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399936} :answer-field/id #uuid "25170187-1ade-556c-bc9b-88b463f1ae2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399934}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d5e9656c-2992-5d25-9ed1-710bfe400433" :question/math-academy-id "q-117084" :question/problem "What is the center and the radius of the circle with equation $(x+5)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=81?$" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's compare the general equation to our equation side-by-side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x+5)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & =81 \\\\ (x-(-5))^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & ={9}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $a=-5,$ $b=3,$ and $r=9.$ \n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(-5,3)$ and its radius is $9.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399940 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e41033f-736e-5607-8753-961b845b539a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-7,-10)$ and the radius is $100$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399942} {:answer/id #uuid "f27f0122-8daa-5b13-a293-2ff7b998ce73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(0,0)$ and the radius is $10$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399943} {:answer/id #uuid "2340cacd-f3c4-5ae7-99ea-d36258840812" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(7,10)$ and the radius is $10$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399944} {:answer/id #uuid "3f33726c-a4cf-5d51-a84c-d3798a16d83e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-7,-10)$ and the radius is $10$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399945} {:answer/id #uuid "a0981346-e334-5ecc-a493-0c31ebc3ef03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(7,10)$ and the radius is $100$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399946}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2340cacd-f3c4-5ae7-99ea-d36258840812" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(7,10)$ and the radius is $10$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399944} :answer-field/id #uuid "62169293-0e81-54fc-944c-cda58edb5a92" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399941}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "064ec2a1-8603-5d8c-96f4-94b94ae469b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-117086" :question/problem "What is the center and the radius of the circle with equation $(x-7)^{2}+(y-10)^{2}=100?$" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's compare the general equation to our equation side-by-side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-7)^{2}+(y-10)^{2} & =100 \\\\ (x-7)^{2}+(y-10)^{2} & ={10}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $a=7,$ $b=10,$ and $r=10.$ \n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(7,10)$ and its radius is $10.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519687 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "120c6703-0634-58a8-a321-af4d885ee95d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=81" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519673} {:answer/id #uuid "5943f4aa-b2e2-5a97-a87c-3b111ac9e761" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-9)^{2}+{y}^{2}=81" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519699} {:answer/id #uuid "e1bccac3-0c41-58e0-9ee1-15518d59a74b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+9)^{2}+{y}^{2}=81" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519722} {:answer/id #uuid "e779ed08-2645-52e9-a03a-13e3b57521fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=324" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519724} {:answer/id #uuid "f2a54f66-6469-5a59-9d1b-a092c3d32eac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519727}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "120c6703-0634-58a8-a321-af4d885ee95d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=81" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519673} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad71d333-d973-53d2-abe1-74b72dc17a5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519714}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "31669fee-6340-55d5-a19f-a1a86dd81325" :question/problem "![](images/56/56e82ecf0aa2a54d7281882c095f3c2b081f719cf3398be20155301d0f0361a0.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overline{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(-9,0)$ and $(9,0)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^2+(y-b)^2=r^2.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(-9,0)$ and $Y(9,0),$ we find that the length of the diameter is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{((-9)-9)^2+(0-0)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-18)^2+(0)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{324+0} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{324} \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{XY}{2}=\\frac{18}{2}=9.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, to find the center we use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{x_1+x_2}{2},\\frac{y_1+y_2}{2})=(\\frac{-9+9}{2},\\frac{0+0}{2})=(0,0)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=9$ and center $(a,b)=(0,0),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^2+(y-b)^2 & =r^2 \\\\ (x-0)^{2}+(y-0)^{2} & =(9)^2 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =81\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519688 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "171998fa-a8e6-54cf-80fe-3036de63fc75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+5)^{2}+(y+4)^{2}=13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519674} {:answer/id #uuid "651dff32-22fe-5869-a86d-9b87382bde3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519703} {:answer/id #uuid "66bdb15e-6b1d-586c-9dde-95f0195f9fec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+6)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519705} {:answer/id #uuid "b54ba1e3-0432-5d2b-a1ec-fc1fd635f071" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+3)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519715} {:answer/id #uuid "bbc53105-6c05-5d72-a4dd-502ef32511be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+3)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519717}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b54ba1e3-0432-5d2b-a1ec-fc1fd635f071" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+3)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519715} :answer-field/id #uuid "5870e946-998f-51a7-bde8-1513faefd91b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519698}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "3d3ac566-19a8-54d2-a32a-fff15a573dbb" :question/problem "![](images/95/95467ab2e67bc1e188a5783ef201859c4e1216f071d6dc21b44adafcba8195c4.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overline{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(-5,-4)$ and $(-1,2)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^2+(y-b)^2=r^2.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(-5,-4)$ and $Y(-1,2),$ we find that the length of the diameter is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{((-5)-(-1))^2+((-4)-2)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^2+(-6)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{52} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4\\cdot 13} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{XY}{2}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{13}}{2}=\\sqrt{13}.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, to find the center we use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{x_1+x_2}{2},\\frac{y_1+y_2}{2})=(\\frac{-5+(-1)}{2},\\frac{-4+2}{2})=(-3,-1)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=\\sqrt{13}$ and center $(a,b)=(-3,-1),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^2+(y-b)^2 & =r^2 \\\\ (x-(-3))^{2}+(y-(-1))^{2} & =(\\sqrt{13})^2 \\\\ (x+3)^{2}+(y+1)^{2} & =13\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519689 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02f0b78b-b7f2-5576-a995-558bca6ff0a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519672} {:answer/id #uuid "1f262cb3-168a-5972-b828-febf492f66cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+6)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519676} {:answer/id #uuid "50fb0255-70cf-5ecb-a1a4-dc8185b2fc80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+3)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519695} {:answer/id #uuid "920ee0b8-9faf-552a-91f9-3be587d126eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+9)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519711} {:answer/id #uuid "a68b3ca5-cfdf-53fa-b851-2ddcfe3fd25e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+3)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=144" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519712}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50fb0255-70cf-5ecb-a1a4-dc8185b2fc80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+3)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519695} :answer-field/id #uuid "62018733-3b56-5178-89ef-816288b19d4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519701}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3e71d13b-143e-5100-ac38-b145c988b060" :question/problem "![](images/4a/4afda0c1af30967941c20c9f70ce926a04e029eedfa605eb3c20d62af8303947.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overline{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(-9,-1)$ and $(3,-1)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^2+(y-b)^2=r^2.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(-9,-1)$ and $Y(3,-1),$ we find that the length of the diameter is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{((-9)-3)^2+((-1)-(-1))^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-12)^2+(0)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144+0} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144} \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{XY}{2}=\\frac{12}{2}=6.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, to find the center we use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{x_1+x_2}{2},\\frac{y_1+y_2}{2})=(\\frac{-9+3}{2},\\frac{-1+(-1)}{2})=(-3,-1)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=6$ and center $(a,b)=(-3,-1),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^2+(y-b)^2 & =r^2 \\\\ (x-(-3))^{2}+(y-(-1))^{2} & =(6)^2 \\\\ (x+3)^{2}+(y+1)^{2} & =36\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519700 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a3f64a6-7826-547e-a7b7-53df738b623f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-7)^{2}+{y}^{2}=49" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519692} {:answer/id #uuid "50de2ef5-ddd9-528e-ab8f-241817f3dca1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=49" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519694} {:answer/id #uuid "55708c35-0697-5f17-b709-5ae8338a0b33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+7)^{2}+{y}^{2}=49" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519696} {:answer/id #uuid "c8d01676-d1ba-5a15-8d7a-8cd472232df9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=196" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519719} {:answer/id #uuid "eb21ace1-79e6-5dbe-a280-1c9fd5977a76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519725}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50de2ef5-ddd9-528e-ab8f-241817f3dca1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=49" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519694} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c5dc3cc-6d23-518e-973a-a46e3aea3a49" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519693}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "60ffb3ff-5c9f-5c7d-98b1-bdc0a2df9a06" :question/problem "![](images/ce/ce6082e3e2563073817e143e8ce91b10c171d0e894d5ed3bea25d925c6fe718f.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overline{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(7,0)$ and $(-7,0)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^2+(y-b)^2=r^2.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(7,0)$ and $Y(-7,0),$ we find that the length of the diameter is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{(7-(-7))^2+(0-0)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(14)^2+(0)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{196+0} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{196} \\\\  & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{XY}{2}=\\frac{14}{2}=7.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, to find the center we use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{x_1+x_2}{2},\\frac{y_1+y_2}{2})=(\\frac{7+(-7)}{2},\\frac{0+0}{2})=(0,0)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=7$ and center $(a,b)=(0,0),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^2+(y-b)^2 & =r^2 \\\\ (x-0)^{2}+(y-0)^{2} & =(7)^2 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =49\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519708 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19ee18de-8c7c-5191-abba-d9e423dbb249" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+(y-4)^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519675} {:answer/id #uuid "2b367407-bcae-513a-b44f-ca4234bd257f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519682} {:answer/id #uuid "2b5d8570-211a-5bfa-a5cd-2ed26e97c918" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186