 & =(3)^2 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519726 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2adb3417-ab63-5657-8903-01b4dc4a2e13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+{y}^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519681} {:answer/id #uuid "4464dc23-ef50-549b-8a55-b20c697f97d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+{y}^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519691} {:answer/id #uuid "64f02e67-b064-5f59-bd9d-187ca8ef0c95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-8)^{2}+{y}^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519702} {:answer/id #uuid "739c144f-3658-510e-99f8-2dcd6514ba59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+{y}^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519706} {:answer/id #uuid "b6127a40-494f-5e5c-87be-b73d338a9555" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519716}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "739c144f-3658-510e-99f8-2dcd6514ba59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+{y}^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519706} :answer-field/id #uuid "20e42abd-473b-542b-bbb5-046316983b2b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519677}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f169aee4-58d1-5815-b8f9-e4167dc8b0c0" :question/problem "![](images/16/16fe72490f7df0dcdd1b3ab78809da1091eccb69a3dda98e3bef08635af322ed.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overline{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(4,2)$ and $(4,-2)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^2+(y-b)^2=r^2.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(4,2)$ and $Y(4,-2),$ we find that the length of the diameter is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{(4-4)^2+(2-(-2))^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(0)^2+(4)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{XY}{2}=\\frac{4}{2}=2.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, to find the center we use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{x_1+x_2}{2},\\frac{y_1+y_2}{2})=(\\frac{4+4}{2},\\frac{2+(-2)}{2})=(4,0)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=2$ and center $(a,b)=(4,0),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^2+(y-b)^2 & =r^2 \\\\ (x-4)^{2}+(y-0)^{2} & =(2)^2 \\\\ (x-4)^{2}+{y}^{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548201 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b2745c4-1441-5995-aaf6-0adbc665aef0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+\\frac{9}{2})^{2}+(y+\\frac{1}{2})^{2}=\\frac{25}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548213} {:answer/id #uuid "37d4082a-8911-5b7c-b50a-10c433cbf0c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+\\frac{9}{2})^{2}+(y-\\frac{1}{2})^{2}=\\frac{25}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548215} {:answer/id #uuid "da3ff54f-5a25-50da-b204-8695bcb437f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-\\frac{9}{2})^{2}+(y+\\frac{1}{2})^{2}=\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548257} {:answer/id #uuid "ea42b5fa-8d2f-550e-9160-d2ffdc3c564b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-\\frac{9}{2})^{2}+(y+\\frac{1}{2})^{2}=\\frac{25}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548262} {:answer/id #uuid "ec1aadba-47b2-5657-83f5-47a149777663" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+\\frac{9}{2})^{2}+(y-\\frac{1}{2})^{2}=\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548264}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37d4082a-8911-5b7c-b50a-10c433cbf0c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+\\frac{9}{2})^{2}+(y-\\frac{1}{2})^{2}=\\frac{25}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548215} :answer-field/id #uuid "16be170c-c7ff-5a97-93c7-1025786aea44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548209}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "0d76f3ef-fa61-505b-b0e2-335ce30237ba" :question/problem "![](images/07/0760173ffa9ede7dc926ff42ddc2a2474433408c2320bc6e37f7dc95ffde2dd1.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(- \\frac{9}{2},\\frac{1}{2})$ and the point $X(-7,3)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{{(-7-\\left(- \\frac{9}{2}\\right))}^{2}+{(3-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\left(- \\frac{5}{2}\\right)^{2}+{\\frac{5}{2}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{25}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-\\left(- \\frac{9}{2}\\right))^{2}+(y-\\frac{1}{2})^{2} & =\\left(\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)^{2} \\\\ (x+\\frac{9}{2})^{2}+(y-\\frac{1}{2})^{2} & =\\frac{25}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548202 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29b47133-63e9-5e3f-aa5f-58a0b6d5b596" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+y^{2}=100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548212} {:answer/id #uuid "3ec27f71-d7bc-5500-837c-5761a7ac8900" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+y^{2}=64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548220} {:answer/id #uuid "5fd614b5-d1e2-5013-98a1-1892641da572" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+y^{2}=100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548229} {:answer/id #uuid "af57762a-cff1-5cc5-a0c6-035779936177" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+y^{2}=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548250} {:answer/id #uuid "e2c14cd4-0321-5ab6-9b82-e326aa414ef5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+9)^{2}+(y+6)^{2}=100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548259}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29b47133-63e9-5e3f-aa5f-58a0b6d5b596" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+y^{2}=100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548212} :answer-field/id #uuid "169b9402-b59d-567f-a7e3-4426f422bb8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548207}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0e569881-0640-5e2f-ad61-f2a974f96814" :question/problem "![](images/6d/6d31b63333aa977b888d7941ac1195bd214201c20606621bb61eb82c81ee1258.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(-1,0)$ and the point $X(-9,-6)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{{(-9-(-1))}^{2}+{(-6-0)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-8)^{2}+(-6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-1))^{2}+(y-0)^{2} & =(10)^{2} \\\\ (x+1)^{2}+y^{2} & =100\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548211 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "142cb5cf-eb17-5a66-bddf-259d1c11d2ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+\\frac{1}{2})^{2}+(y-\\frac{5}{2})^{2}=\\frac{49}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548205} {:answer/id #uuid "598a7dfc-10dc-5ab3-9d18-c3cf3f01773e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-\\frac{1}{2})^{2}+(y+\\frac{5}{2})^{2}=\\frac{7\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548226} {:answer/id #uuid "679c2f50-d4ed-5457-be54-4c6140240698" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+\\frac{1}{2})^{2}+(y-\\frac{5}{2})^{2}=\\frac{7\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548231} {:answer/id #uuid "74cfed18-39c2-5554-8a0a-adc370f4e424" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-\\frac{1}{2})^{2}+(y+\\frac{5}{2})^{2}=\\frac{49}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548235} {:answer/id #uuid "c334d9c2-5306-529f-bcff-4b35925d958a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+\\frac{1}{2})^{2}+(y+\\frac{5}{2})^{2}=\\frac{49}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548253}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "142cb5cf-eb17-5a66-bddf-259d1c11d2ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+\\frac{1}{2})^{2}+(y-\\frac{5}{2})^{2}=\\frac{49}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548205} :answer-field/id #uuid "60dba049-c375-5187-a142-54d6efdc2595" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548230}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "23cb419e-0b3f-54ac-b7c2-ccc117d54760" :question/problem "![](images/d0/d0ed7e0b3302ef2debc3e5662c51b7e10aa5ca41c55aabdde16f89e78181a96e.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(- \\frac{1}{2},\\frac{5}{2})$ and the point $X(-4,-1)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{{(-4-\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right))}^{2}+{(-1-\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\left(- \\frac{7}{2}\\right)^{2}+\\left(- \\frac{7}{2}\\right)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right))^{2}+(y-\\frac{5}{2})^{2} & =\\left(\\frac{7\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)^{2} \\\\ (x+\\frac{1}{2})^{2}+(y-\\frac{5}{2})^{2} & =\\frac{49}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548216 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b0ae84e-7f5d-510c-83b2-3177805b0468" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-\\frac{9}{2})^{2}+(y-\\frac{1}{2})^{2}=\\frac{41}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548210} {:answer/id #uuid "8121e814-633e-581b-87a3-1b1a2141d2bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+\\frac{9}{2})^{2}+(y+\\frac{1}{2})^{2}=\\frac{\\sqrt{82}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548239} {:answer/id #uuid "9aeb601b-cad5-512f-9ea8-2855c4a40d6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-\\frac{9}{2})^{2}+(y-\\frac{1}{2})^{2}=\\frac{\\sqrt{82}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548246} {:answer/id #uuid "a2ae6e9a-0bbf-5c7f-9636-e29b0935a5a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "