on/id #uuid "8deaaef8-3b38-5fd8-8c73-aba47ef905b0" :question/problem "![](images/fc/fc322a5919f391bab61e491e555096b60697b9c17f2a88851348a552470206a4.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(5,0)$ and the point $X(11,8)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{{(11-5)}^{2}+{(8-0)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{8}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-5)^{2}+(y-0)^{2} & =(10)^{2} \\\\ (x-5)^{2}+y^{2} & =100\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548261 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f7a4ea2-e3e8-57c0-aa17-e56dd3409c3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+3)^{2}+y^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548203} {:answer/id #uuid "14d67f72-f7d3-5a53-ad86-2ea511613b09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548206} {:answer/id #uuid "3be1a314-eabc-562a-99f5-98ee3ac84f1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+y^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548218} {:answer/id #uuid "826691e9-a9af-55e9-b707-724cadecfa4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+3)^{2}+y^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548240} {:answer/id #uuid "8f8dd643-3e61-554e-9ff0-c52a6c39c3cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+3)^{2}+y^{2}=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548244}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "826691e9-a9af-55e9-b707-724cadecfa4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+3)^{2}+y^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548240} :answer-field/id #uuid "92c6ea21-ae94-5c5b-afe4-586087f48065" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548245}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e7dbeeb0-66df-5321-a92b-7343842382ce" :question/problem "![](images/14/14636b213a29b8ed188cb8020776cca59deb42ffa3daffc8df7f8b757c4c0fd3.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(-3,0)$ and the point $X(1,-3)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{{(1-(-3))}^{2}+{(-3-0)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-3))^{2}+(y-0)^{2} & =(5)^{2} \\\\ (x+3)^{2}+y^{2} & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554915 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "079ab703-3494-529d-afba-bcf7c8521c6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(- \\frac{3}{2},-7)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{6}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554917} {:answer/id #uuid "180a802f-f527-576f-bb15-bc897139ed79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(\\frac{3}{2},7)$ and radius is $6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554922} {:answer/id #uuid "35d5d362-3d29-570d-8c81-37dc1bf2e964" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(- \\frac{3}{2},7)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{6}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554927} {:answer/id #uuid "9672e88d-f6f9-587d-ae31-56fac9e1d295" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(\\frac{3}{2},-7)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{6}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554957} {:answer/id #uuid "a8419079-e366-5a9c-a724-3f829a0054d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(\\frac{3}{2},7)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{6}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554961}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8419079-e366-5a9c-a724-3f829a0054d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(\\frac{3}{2},7)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{6}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554961} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b5bda28-14b4-5ec3-a2af-fa277a15f98d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554924}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "01985a4a-805a-5dc1-8f8a-acd45ccb338a" :question/problem "What is the center and radius of the circle with equation $(x-\\frac{3}{2})^{2}+(y-7)^{2}=6?$" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's compare the general equation to our equation side-by-side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-\\frac{3}{2})^{2}+(y-7)^{2} & =6 \\\\ (x-\\frac{3}{2})^{2}+(y-7)^{2} & =(\\sqrt{6})^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $a=\\frac{3}{2},$ $b=7,$ and $r=\\sqrt{6}.$ \n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(\\frac{3}{2},7)$ and its radius is $\\sqrt{6}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554932 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "273abafe-ba93-5ef4-b7d7-548062af84f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(\\frac{1}{3},8)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{6}$" :