cture, we see that our circle is centered at $C(3,4)$ and the radius of the circle is $r=\\frac{7}{4}.$ Therefore, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-3)^{2}+(y-4)^{2} & =\\left(\\frac{7}{4}\\right)^{2} \\\\ (x-3)^{2}+(y-4)^{2} & =\\frac{49}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561460 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31b4e07c-43c7-5b7c-86ee-bbfbee73b3e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=\\frac{196}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561470} {:answer/id #uuid "7b7b0fb9-b54d-5dce-b02b-884703b0e99f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=\\frac{196}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561492} {:answer/id #uuid "82c8d150-23b7-54fa-8871-76b7ff7365f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=\\frac{196}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561496} {:answer/id #uuid "ae6ad6ce-84a0-5d0e-9f6b-72cac338cc26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=\\frac{196}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561506} {:answer/id #uuid "f8e6952d-91f1-517e-8c30-5095b978f727" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=\\frac{14}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561522}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b7b0fb9-b54d-5dce-b02b-884703b0e99f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=\\frac{196}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561492} :answer-field/id #uuid "220fac2c-89c5-51d1-aa4d-d4ae66fbb1b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561464}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1d65a625-1ad4-5ef2-8b76-a65fd658c912" :question/problem "![](images/18/1893e7f4fa7b6b3927a3b3750f526a747b4be615f91a60a446231df0b4bf8a91.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the circle given above?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFrom the picture, we see that our circle is centered at $C(2,3)$ and the radius of the circle is $r=\\frac{14}{3}.$ Therefore, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & =\\left(\\frac{14}{3}\\right)^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & =\\frac{196}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561465 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75abbf65-1902-5344-828d-f2979f123894" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-\\frac{17}{4})^{2}+(y+\\frac{23}{4})^{2}=\\frac{81}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561486} {:answer/id #uuid "8b3e6896-9408-5411-9efa-d8cb0f877d55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+\\frac{17}{4})^{2}+(y-\\frac{23}{4})^{2}=\\frac{81}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561500} {:answer/id #uuid "bbfd8876-cf93-555f-b033-970f615348ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+\\frac{17}{4})^{2}+(y+\\frac{23}{4})^{2}=\\frac{81}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561510} {:answer/id #uuid "c27c5584-8c61-5764-ac6b-4eab0311c534" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-\\frac{17}{4})^{2}+(y+\\frac{23}{4})^{2}=\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561511} {:answer/id #uuid "c56910fc-16e8-506e-85cc-9531fbee8443" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-\\frac{17}{4})^{2}+(y-\\frac{23}{4})^{2}=\\frac{81}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561513}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75abbf65-19