swer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-6)^{2}+{y}^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643408}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ade58e31-34f8-5983-b93e-8283e7bd0def" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+(y+6)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643402} :answer-field/id #uuid "deff8e78-47cc-5759-a937-c8914abe94e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643409}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fef50ed7-191f-5f76-9cd3-699de213a250" :question/problem "![](images/d9/d9ff685b5298b604bd7fd03012e98a2237346e4eade41c27d0561d9f2b540db3.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the circle given above?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFrom the picture, we see that our circle is centered at $C(0,-6)$ and the radius of the circle is $r=2.$ Therefore, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-0)^{2}+(y-(-6))^{2} & ={2}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+(y+6)^{2} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643421 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cb1db82-268d-5616-9a16-71ea7171deae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-5,9)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643420} {:answer/id #uuid "b596ce15-98b5-5472-83cf-5d5f18cc9d37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(0,0)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643439} {:answer/id #uuid "c1f61d8b-4b36-52fd-ac19-6f263fc1d40b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(5,9)$ and radius is $\\frac{1}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643441} {:answer/id #uuid "c581c4fc-b4ba-592c-9be7-575964af3cff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-5,-9)$ and radius is $\\frac{1}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643444} {:answer/id #uuid "c75436fa-9ef3-519d-839c-53f55a738940" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(5,-9)$ and radius is $\\frac{1}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643445}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0cb1db82-268d-5616-9a16-71ea7171deae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-5,9)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643420} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bf8e667-9628-56dd-a9c6-27d22795f689" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643419}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "117379ed-80be-5781-87d9-96c4fbba0289" :question/problem "What is the center and radius of the circle with equation $(x+5)^{2}+(y-9)^{2}=2$?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's compare the general equation to our equation side-by-side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x+5)^{2}+(y-9)^{2} & =2 \\\\ (x-(-5))^{2}+(y-9)^{2} & =(\\sqrt{2})^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $a=-5,$ $b=9,$ and $r=\\sqrt{2}.$ \n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(-5,9)$ and its radius is $\\sqrt{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643425 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0693a403-a4cb-5c2a-a911-b70b149c60ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(0,0)$ and radius is $7$" :db/id #edb/ref 1759218664341