tered at $(-3,4)$ and its radius is $7.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643429 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1851b0de-60ac-59e3-b62f-4b2f715bb037" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-6,2)$ and radius is $10$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643423} {:answer/id #uuid "5644a776-e73e-5083-8ac3-43154c63c9c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(6,-2)$ and radius is $\\frac{1}{100}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643426} {:answer/id #uuid "8694025e-3a3f-5d9f-98ba-8cc1e995052b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(6,2)$ and radius is $\\frac{1}{100}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643432} {:answer/id #uuid "dbec6ab8-68ae-5fbb-8518-bd02d0841180" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-6,-2)$ and radius is $10$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643449} {:answer/id #uuid "fda1263a-c897-53af-a924-ac4969a27c62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(6,-2)$ and radius is $10$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643451}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fda1263a-c897-53af-a924-ac4969a27c62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(6,-2)$ and radius is $10$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643451} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd2297b4-8cd6-55e2-8a50-c92f0c38d00d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643446}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6901ef44-3d09-5e7b-9745-7585a9bbef8d" :question/problem "What is the center and radius of the circle with equation $(x-6)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=100$?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's compare the general equation to our equation side-by-side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-6)^{2}+(y+2)^{2} & =100 \\\\ (x-6)^{2}+(y-(-2))^{2} & ={10}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $a=6,$ $b=-2,$ and $r=10.$ \n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(6,-2)$ and its radius is $10.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643431 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "786b378a-3427-5d93-9bbd-ce9ecb472fdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(1,10)$ and radius is $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643430} {:answer/id #uuid "9c1c414e-097e-50a0-9dd8-95394e55ecf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(1,10)$ and radius is $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643433} {:answer/id #uuid "b26c26d9-9365-5994-b91a-365d6e586e99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-1,-10)$ and radius is $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643438} {:answer/id #uuid "c3912159-1601-5962-9c2b-68f7eb10cb96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-1,10)$ and radius is $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643443} {:answer/id #uuid "ffb6149f-a67f-57a8-a60e-16769fa2be43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-1,10)$ and radius is $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643452}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c1c414e-097e-50a0-9dd8-95394e55ecf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(1,10)$ and radius is $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643433} :answer-field/id #uuid "d886616f-8582-580b-8a46-f971c1e5cb8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643448}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7d391c4d-f3ee-52b5-98d1-d5bf9490746d" :question/problem "What is the center and radius of the circle with equation $(x-1)^{2}+(y-10)^{2}=4$?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's compare the general equation to our equation side-by-side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+(y-10)^{2} & =4 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+(y-10)^{2} & ={2}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $a=1,$ $b=10,$ and $r=2.$ \n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(1,10)$ and its radius is $2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643447 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1313e4e6-726f-59c1-842c-db11adaa10d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-1,-3)$ and radius is $\\frac{1}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643422} {:answer/id #uuid "27561817-eafa-5919-b8fc-6de1daf0b4ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(1,-3)$ and radius is $\\frac{1}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643424} {:answer/id #uuid "a6686ecc-217b-5c2b-b281-90dd71d84233" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(0,0)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643436} {:answer/id #uuid "af85d51a-c8a6-56c1-909f-dfdd1e2839cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-1,3)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643437} {:answer/id #uuid "bb559550-0832-535c-b67b-db5930ca8354" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(1,3)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643440}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af85d51a-c8a6-56c1-909f-dfdd1e2839cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-1,3)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643437} :answer-field/id #uuid "a58bdad6-014d-5c79-a37f-e1a807d94d10" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643434}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d036a794-3814-5530-98e7-0471c43aa78f" :question/problem "What is the center and radius of the circle with equation $(x+1)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=2$?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's compare the general equation to our equation side-by-side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x+1)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & =2 \\\\ (x-(-1))^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & =(\\sqrt{2})^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $a=-1,$ $b=3,$ and $r=\\sqrt{2}.$ \n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(-1,3)$ and its radius is $\\sqrt{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186644239 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18a5d4d0-8dab-5abd-9fb4-d11e1c39a6e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y-4)^{2}=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644240} {:answer/id #uuid "1cab2ed4-5de3-5103-bbae-95a118838b2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y+4)^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644241} {:answer/id #uuid "6915ac2f-2cb5-5d40-aade-8e631af6ef0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y+4)^{2}=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644250} {:answer/id #uuid "6d99810c-7a61-508d-8288-61424db20dcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y-4)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644252} {:answer/id #uuid "88c4ccca-5214-5665-8a53-cd6bb1ef03f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y+4)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644256}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d99810c-7a61-508d-8288-61424db20dcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y-4)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644252} :answer-field/id #uuid "c96de200-4a76-5927-a8bb-187a51da2a78" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644265}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1277d88d-eaff-548c-b792-74996ecc56b5" :question/problem "![](images/da/dafe3c837094d2b683e6d67b7ea267b4105935b47ebcc5f9e5c05a6cb67bfa69.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overline{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(-2,4)$ and $(-6,4)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^2+(y-b)^2=r^2.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(-2,4)$ and $Y(-6,4),$ we find that the length of the diameter is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{((-2)-(-6))^2+(4-4)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(4)^2+(0)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+0} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{XY}{2}=\\frac{4}{2}=2.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, to find the center we use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{x_1+x_2}{2},\\frac{y_1+y_2}{2})=(\\frac{-2+(-6)}{2},\\frac{4+4}{2})=(-4,4)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=2$ and center $(a,b)=(-4,4),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^2+(y-b)^2 & =r^2 \\\\ (x-(-4))^{2}+(y-4)^{2} & =(2)^2 \\\\ (x+4)^{2}+(y-4)^{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186644243 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b89de45-5c82-57d0-929e-ed84987ef9cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644237} {:answer/id #uuid "1012cfc4-4214-57fc-ae8e-9fff64632845" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644238} {:answer/id #uuid "7e6ec6f5-605c-55df-90e0-50d0569d0d44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+(y-4)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644253} {:answer/id #uuid "9f3fd789-d8ac-57e6-9a7f-8060f7d273cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+(y-4)^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644260} {:answer/id #uuid "f892cacd-68fb-5563-8c11-ef758f7492fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644271}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e6ec6f5-605c-55df-90e0-50d0569d0d44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+(y-4)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644253} :answer-field/id #uuid "680d2c62-22a6-560b-b8cb-4d16b9a53697" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644248}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "39a693ad-171a-5a97-9bed-2d78bc2269b3" :question/problem "![](images/65/65981cc51d368435e242beb73049477b2ec4e1f66a6873391e2b80562f37afc9.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overline{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(3,6)$ and $(3,2)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^2+(y-b)^2=r^2.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(3,6)$ and $Y(3,2),$ we find that the length of the diameter is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{(3-3)^2+(6-2)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(0)^2+(4)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{XY}{2}=\\frac{4}{2}=2.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, to find the center we use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{x_1+x_2}{2},\\frac{y_1+y_2}{2})=(\\frac{3+3}{2},\\frac{6+2}{2})=(3,4)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=2$ and center $(a,b)=(3,4),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^2+(y-b)^2 & =r^2 \\\\ (x-3)^{2}+(y-4)^{2} & =(2)^2 \\\\ (x-3)^{2}+(y-4)^{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186644245 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "624c9169-a7b1-502e-a6e3-507762e5d2c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y+5)^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644246} {:answer/id #uuid "85a8bc13-e97a-5436-8349-a0e340c09fff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y-5)^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644255} {:answer/id #uuid "8c93714c-6433-5762-b55a-2983f4bf85ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y+5)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644258} {:answer/id #uuid "d348dfcf-7aeb-5aa0-a1dd-632e44291f59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y+5)^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644268} {:answer/id #uuid "d8cc8946-e790-57f1-ad6d-8292c20a4f49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y-5)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644269}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "624c9169-a7b1-502e-a6e3-507762e5d2c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y+5)^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644246} :answer-field/id #uuid "6819fd4f-7f2e-54c0-a34e-70d7140eda5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644249}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4319db8e-dbfa-58c6-ac81-99cd0181a920" :question/problem "![](images/b5/b564348aaed279585e1025b0e0d4f77a8b84cd659be3e7702ee3590ff9016217.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overline{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(5,-5)$ and $(-3,-5)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^2+(y-b)^2=r^2.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(5,-5)$ and $Y(-3,-5),$ we find that the length of the diameter is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{(5-(-3))^2+((-5)-(-5))^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(8)^2+(0)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64+0} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64} \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{XY}{2}=\\frac{8}{2}=4.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, to find the center we use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{x_1+x_2}{2},\\frac{y_1+y_2}{2})=(\\frac{5+(-3)}{2},\\frac{-5+(-5)}{2})=(1,-5)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=4$ and center $(a,b)=(1,-5),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^2+(y-b)^2 & =r^2 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+(y-(-5))^{2} & =(4)^2 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+(y+5)^{2} & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186644254 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b86ddcf-19e0-5401-8caa-63164b00d79f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644244} {:answer/id #uuid "6d5ab7de-9006-5b00-9397-0915db29e3d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644251} {:answer/id #uuid "a7536983-17b8-5762-b999-94838e988b3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644261} {:answer/id #uuid "ae6719e7-ffc4-5457-989f-b17381e562c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644262} {:answer/id #uuid "b117f187-464e-5ca2-93a1-7179ffdb94c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644263}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d5ab7de-9006-5b00-9397-0915db29e3d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644251} :answer-field/id #uuid "66ac4793-4158-567c-b344-dc0abc1f5650" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644247}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7ebafd3a-69ea-5188-a0b3-fb6fdf04c0dc" :question/problem "![](images/25/25881bcaea3899a61dbbea369276ec417e9ee4f89f3a6b4d4c5082186131eb34.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overline{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(8,-2)$ and $(0,-2)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^2+(y-b)^2=r^2.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(8,-2)$ and $Y(0,-2),$ we find that the length of the diameter is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{(8-0)^2+((-2)-(-2))^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(8)^2+(0)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64+0} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64} \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{XY}{2}=\\frac{8}{2}=4.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, to find the center we use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{x_1+x_2}{2},\\frac{y_1+y_2}{2})=(\\frac{8+0}{2},\\frac{-2+(-2)}{2})=(4,-2)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=4$ and center $(a,b)=(4,-2),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^2+(y-b)^2 & =r^2 \\\\ (x-4)^{2}+(y-(-2))^{2} & =(4)^2 \\\\ (x-4)^{2}+(y+2)^{2} & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186644267 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "387ba057-9444-5ac2-95d4-df63aa4aee14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y-4)^{2}=36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644242} {:answer/id #uuid "938420b3-3f8c-51ed-8047-95794a3feb48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y+4)^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644259} {:answer/id #uuid "c6f37562-fafc-5dca-a4d3-577e28ee9c40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y+4)^{2}=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644264} {:answer/id #uuid "cddf6ad5-70aa-5dc6-ad9c-d91ac7c4db32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y-4)^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644266} {:answer/id #uuid "dade316d-5af8-5774-ab19-3c59f3bfe6a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y+4)^{2}=36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644270}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cddf6ad5-70aa-5dc6-ad9c-d91ac7c4db32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y-4)^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644266} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c731100-4b72-504a-819b-6d6e9cf4f094" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644257}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d114b42c-0345-5d95-a864-5d3b7695fc69" :question/problem "![](images/3a/3a7b210d9f5174075b6fa5c47cbd3857449930116bebe70ba73342e146b95e6e.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overline{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(-4,5)$ and $(-4,3)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^2+(y-b)^2=r^2.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(-4,5)$ and $Y(-4,3),$ we find that the length of the diameter is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{((-4)-(-4))^2+(5-3)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(0)^2+(2)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{XY}{2}=\\frac{2}{2}=1.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, to find the center we use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{x_1+x_2}{2},\\frac{y_1+y_2}{2})=(\\frac{-4+(-4)}{2},\\frac{5+3}{2})=(-4,4)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=1$ and center $(a,b)=(-4,4),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^2+(y-b)^2 & =r^2 \\\\ (x-(-4))^{2}+(y-4)^{2} & =(1)^2 \\\\ (x+4)^{2}+(y-4)^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186644274 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1688acce-375b-5821-bdcb-0881e9162e15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644275} {:answer/id #uuid "3b20971d-90b7-5e1a-a7d6-62ab0adf8db5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644283} {:answer/id #uuid "5b8c8d64-1633-5ba5-ab18-1f902ee6786f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=74" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644290} {:answer/id #uuid "97420ec6-5165-5bf3-9405-eda53bb51b6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=68" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644297} {:answer/id #uuid "a681a029-9fd3-5fc4-b794-ae75f6346c98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=74" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644300}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b8c8d64-1633-5ba5-ab18-1f902ee6786f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=74" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644290} :answer-field/id #uuid "17b68f3d-d10c-571e-8fb5-c7f8b2efcb7b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644276}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0a9a6ebd-ee93-5096-b736-a976f237efb6" :question/problem "![](images/41/41e5667e2c8ac5ea137ea1fc4ccc95853e76bf73623554d65457d566129dd03e.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(2,1)$ and the point $X(7,-6)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{{(7-2)}^{2}+{(-6-1)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+(-7)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{74}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y-1)^{2} & =(\\sqrt{74})^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y-1)^{2} & =74\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186644285 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e44cd95-2d59-5899-ba00-4e6d4028f6be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y-5)^{2}=53" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644287} {:answer/id #uuid "b3053370-9d6b-58ce-9692-772a0f08ee9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y+5)^{2}=53" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644302} {:answer/id #uuid "cb544d6e-fc3a-5ef2-804f-f3b092bbd068" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y+5)^{2}=61" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644304} {:answer/id #uuid "d4786bfb-a815-598b-9a9f-6b9e7857730b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y+5)^{2}=26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644305} {:answer/id #uuid "fceb2302-c5e2-575a-a12f-bdff6e700872" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y-5)^{2}=61" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644307}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fceb2302-c5e2-575a-a12f-bdff6e700872" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y-5)^{2}=61" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644307} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b940a5e-b049-5de8-b66b-cefa2e190f01" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644294}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3cd23c8f-314c-5023-8e66-56baa2d8360e" :question/problem "![](images/34/342d9e97733b5eb453b703bc38757e5d5a1c94881c28f5d85c3809e3648566ce.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(-1,5)$ and the point $X(-6,-1)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{{(-6-(-1))}^{2}+{(-1-5)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+(-6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{61}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-1))^{2}+(y-5)^{2} & =(\\sqrt{61})^{2} \\\\ (x+1)^{2}+(y-5)^{2} & =61\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186644292 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "195c1b57-1093-5536-a5d0-65412180bf31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644277} {:answer/id #uuid "3d02339f-b486-5c50-a7fe-9d733f2fb5bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644286} {:answer/id #uuid "5b4aa4ff-7c01-5a03-b7b8-699a1ce80a15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644289} {:answer/id #uuid "9c309fbc-f19d-59f5-b373-a9f035dc0e61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644298} {:answer/id #uuid "a97ba540-d7f7-5302-a843-6c87a6e205c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644301}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d02339f-b486-5c50-a7fe-9d733f2fb5bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644286} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cddea0e-5cf3-5779-aaf4-41d1d77b4461" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644278}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "69bce459-fc52-5839-9976-16b9ea50bf15" :question/problem "![](images/fd/fd0281b7eaed1b648e725b437b362da1268f3dfaf2e2c324d94c45f8bd9aed77.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(-2,-1)$ and the point $X(4,5)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{(4-(-2))^{2}+(5-(-1))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-2))^{2}+(y-(-1))^{2} & ={(6\\sqrt{2})}^{2} \\\\ (x+2)^{2}+(y+1)^{2} & =72\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186644295 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "060607e2-f9ef-5b76-a5de-082146d2f4aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=53" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644273} {:answer/id #uuid "3886f8a2-1321-5345-b884-90d18e4db2c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=53" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644282} {:answer/id #uuid "5f0e2b09-87c1-5cc9-9d0d-41da368a174c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644291} {:answer/id #uuid "6b4b92a8-a703-5552-969e-7218911f42d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644293} {:answer/id #uuid "9f8418be-9879-5215-84ed-811d9963d675" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644299}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "060607e2-f9ef-5b76-a5de-082146d2f4aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=53" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644273} :answer-field/id #uuid "375bcac1-b404-5ee3-a8ed-44ab3ebea3cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644281}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "763d752d-339b-56d1-b868-a0ba61605799" :question/problem "![](images/cd/cd37fcb3ef9e8e000ec8da12e8fda150e30cff16cfe96f4a6dec14af725b3a2e.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(4,3)$ and the point $X(6,-4)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{{(6-4)}^{2}+{(-4-3)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-7)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{53}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & =(\\sqrt{53})^{2} \\\\ (x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & =53\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186644303 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d738195-a44d-5a47-8b90-b13f616c2b36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644279} {:answer/id #uuid "3616a475-6a3c-50be-8000-05a2d4d4efdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644280} {:answer/id #uuid "3cac3ae8-6c54-53e7-8439-2d0f7f69e8d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=61" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644284} {:answer/id #uuid "4f2c165e-e319-5b53-ba39-123911b97314" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644288} {:answer/id #uuid "8b4d939d-ec15-55e3-b9ff-8494da3c6ddb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644296}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b4d939d-ec15-55e3-b9ff-8494da3c6ddb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644296} :answer-field/id #uuid "eff7ed69-a87a-524c-8832-666a17c9fbf4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644306}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c175fc0b-06b3-5971-ad14-b067ea7cf64b" :question/problem "![](images/c1/c1da4ee77880bb0c8ece506cf794fc30d4a4176f121374d020b46609c3bd01d1.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(-2,2)$ and the point $X(1,-3)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{{(1-(-2))}^{2}+{(-3-2)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{34}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-2))^{2}+(y-2)^{2} & =(\\sqrt{34})^{2} \\\\ (x+2)^{2}+(y-2)^{2} & =34\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
